title: Exported functions and shared types/classes/interfaces flagged as unused
updated_at: "2026-08-31T08:55:25Z"
---
## Expected Behavior

Declarations that are part of a plugin's cross-plugin surface must never
be reported unused by the unused-declaration analysis:

- functions exported via info.toml `[script] exports` / import-signature
  files, and
- `shared` types — classes, interfaces, enums (and shared funcdefs /
  shared global functions) — which dependent plugins consume via the
  AngelScript shared-entity mechanism without any textual reference
  inside this workspace.

## Actual Behavior

`src/analysis/unused.rs` exempts export FILE paths and (B062) roots the
signatures named in strict export files (`import <sig> from "Mod";`).
The `shared` keyword on a declaration is never consulted — the only
`shared` mentions in the module are the `shared_exports` *path* set. A
`shared class` / `shared interface` / `shared enum` declared in an
ordinary (non-export) source file, unreferenced within the plugin
itself, is flagged unused even though its whole purpose is consumption
by dependent plugins. Exported functions whose shape B062's
signature-rooting doesn't reach can be hit the same way.

## Mechanism / Fix Sketch

Treat the `shared` modifier as a usage root: any declaration carrying
`shared` (and members reachable from it, per the existing rooting rules)
is exempt from unused reporting. Verify the parser/AST records the
`shared` modifier; if it is currently dropped at parse time, that is
part of this bug. Exported functions should be rooted whether they reach
the analysis via strict-export signature rooting or export-file
exemption — cover the seams between the two.

## Test Cases (generalize per repo convention)

Positive (must NOT warn):
- `shared class Foo {}` unreferenced in-plugin
- `shared interface IFoo {}` unreferenced
- `shared enum EFoo {}` unreferenced
- shared funcdef / shared global function, if the grammar allows
- function listed in a strict `[script] exports` import-signature file
- function defined in an exports file exempted by path

Negative controls (MUST still warn):
- identical non-shared class/interface/enum, unreferenced
- non-exported unreferenced function alongside the exported one

